  "id": "Compound::DB00172 - Gene::55214",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between L-proline and P3h2, mediated through the enzyme activity of procollagen-proline 3-dioxygenase and peptidyl-proline 3-dioxygenase. L-proline binds to P3h3 or P3h1, which in turn participate in the catalytic activity of these enzymes. Both pathways ultimately lead to P3h2 being involved in the same biological process. The scores from the paths indicate a strong, though slightly varying, connection between L-proline and P3h2, likely due to the overlapping roles of the enzymes in the same metabolic pathway. The evidence supports a mechanism where L-proline acts as a substrate or inhibitor, influencing the activity of these enzymes, which in turn affects P3h2. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for L-proline in modulating the activity of these enzymes, possibly through direct interaction or by influencing their regulatory mechanisms.",
